# Comparisons do not chain; the help rewrites the chain with and.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | where a < b < c
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..25
  PIPELINE@0..24
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..24
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      BIN_EXPR@15..24
        BIN_EXPR@15..20
          NAME_REF@15..16
            IDENT@15..16 "a"
          WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
          LT@17..18 "<"
          WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
          NAME_REF@19..20
            IDENT@19..20 "b"
        WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
        LT@21..22 "<"
        WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
        NAME_REF@23..24
          IDENT@23..24 "c"
  WHITESPACE@24..25 "\n"

error[DS0101]: comparison operators cannot be chained
  --> query:1:22
  |
1 | from t | where a < b < c
  |                ----- ^ a second comparison
  |                |
  |                the result of this comparison is not a value to compare again
  |
  = help: compare each pair separately: `a < b and b < c`
